                        jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                        sling:resourceType="sumit/components/text"
                        text="&lt;p>The most important part is to see what type of skateboard is the one for you. Here are a few tips to look at before you buy your skateboard:&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>Standard - See if you are a beginner, intermediate or an expert. For beginners - The skateboard for beginners is slightly smaller in size and the slanted bearings limit the speed to limit the risk of falling which is perfect for kids. It helps them learn to balance on the skateboard. For kids who want to learn a few tricks, the mid 3 beginners’ skateboard is perfect because of its steering components such as trucks, wheels, and bearings.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>Technical Skateboards - The mid 5 skateboard is sturdy and helps the kids learn tricks and is perfect for intermediates as well. The team skateboard is dynamic, fast, manoeuvrable, and allows riders to perform all the tricks. This skateboard is designed for teenagers and adults who are experts in skateboarding.&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;p>Now buy skateboards online from our website!&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;"
                        textIsRich="true"/>
